   "prereq": "§4-52: Use the tests shown in Table 4-3 to isolate problems to the major functional circuit groups of the 732A. It is assumed that the external symptoms given in Table 4-2 have been examined and that the primary circuit of the power transformer is operable. This procedure is conducted with the instrument energized, observe the previously stated WARNINGS and CAUTIONS. Table 4-3 footnotes: * Voltage measurements taken with Multimeter A, except for those marked with *** in corrective action column. ** Conditions: battery installed, BATTERY OPR switch ON. *** Calibration of 10V output affects calibration of this output. Each step names the board the points are on; the first point is taken as the meter's HI lead, the second as its LO lead - Table 4-3 does not say so; it is inferred from §4-44 steps 7 and 14 (\"TP5 is positive with respect to TP1\", \"TP2 is positive with respect to TP1\") and the nets on Figures 8-3 / 8-4. Table 4-3 prints no tolerances - the ones offered here are assumed and marked inferred.",
