   "prereq": "§4-31: Use the following procedure to verify that the instrument is operational. The required test equipment is listed in Table 4-1. Equivalent instruments may be used, provided the minimum specification is met. (Table 4-1 marks for procedure A: Certified 732A - Fluke 732A; Four to Nine Cell Bank of Standard Cells - Guildline 9152P/4 or 9; Multimeter A - Fluke 8050A/8060A, 4½-digit display, 20 kΩ resistance range, 200 mV to 200V ac or dc; Adjustment Tool - Fluke P/N 686113. The Load Resistor 1 kΩ ½W Carbon Composition, Fluke P/N 108597, that step 5 uses is marked B, D in the table, not A.) §4-3: perform the acceptance test upon receipt of the instrument. §4-4 NOTE: use Fluke Low Thermal EMF Cable or copper wire with crimped and soldered low-thermal lugs clamped in the binding posts for all interconnections; avoid ordinary nickel-plated banana plugs. CAUTION: to avoid cracking the plastic binding post insulator, tighten only with finger pressure. Do not use tools.",
